# Build outputs
/pulse
/pulse.exe
/bin/

# Test artifacts
*.test
*.out
coverage.txt

# Local state (never committed; secrets never touch disk by design)
.pulse/

# Agent-environment vendoring (ponytail plugin + third-party skills).
# Restore with the installers in ~/.local/share/opencode-skill-src/ (MEMORY.md ADL-0013).
.opencode/
opencode.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Markdown lockdown
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AGENTS.md §4.6 defines a COMPLETE documentation surface: seven Essential Vibe
# Coding Files and nothing else. Ignoring *.md by default makes that structural
# rather than aspirational — a stray notes file, a scratch README inside a test
# fixture directory, or a vendored third-party README cannot be committed by
# accident, and cannot be mistaken for state a reviewer is expected to read.
#
# The default-deny is the point. A repository that lists what it tracks is a
# repository where every unlisted file is a decision nobody made; a repository
# that lists what it does NOT track is one where every tracked file was.
#
# Two git semantics decide whether this rule actually does what it looks like
# it does. Both were verified by `git check-ignore` rather than assumed, and
# the first one was WRONG on the first attempt:
#
#   1. A `!pattern` containing no slash matches at EVERY depth. An unanchored
#      `!README.md` therefore resurrects `vendor/README.md` and
#      testdata/fixture/README.md — which is the precise thing this rule
#      exists to prevent. Every negation below is anchored with a leading
#      slash so it matches only at the repository root.
#   2. A `!pattern` cannot rescue a file whose parent DIRECTORY is excluded,
#      because git never descends into an excluded directory. No directory is
#      excluded here, so root negations apply normally.
*.md

# --- the seven Essential Vibe Coding Files (AGENTS.md §4.6) ---
# DESIGN_SYSTEM.md is whitelisted alongside the other six DELIBERATELY. It is
# the TUI aesthetics and keybinding contract, it is one of the seven, and a
# whitelist that omitted it would untrack a mandated document — the exact
# failure the default-deny above exists to prevent, reintroduced through the
# exception list.
!/AGENTS.md
!/PRD.md
!/ARCHITECTURE.md
!/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md
!/ROADMAP.md
!/TASKS.md
!/MEMORY.md

# --- skill-agent configuration (MEMORY.md ADL-0026) ---
# These three are NOT part of the seven Essential Vibe Coding Files. They are
# read by the engineering skills (triage, to-spec, to-tickets, domain-modeling)
# and mean nothing to the compiler, so they are whitelisted narrowly rather than
# by loosening the default-deny above.
#
# `/.agents/*.md` is anchored AND single-star ON PURPOSE. Git semantics that
# made this subtle are documented in the header: an unanchored `!` matches at
# every depth, and a single `*` does not cross a `/`. So this line whitelists
# exactly the three config files sitting directly in `.agents/` and leaves the
# ~40 vendored SKILL.md files underneath `.agents/skills/` ignored. Untracking
# the vendor tree is the existing policy for `.opencode/` (ADL-0013/0014): it is
# reproducible from `skills-lock.json` plus the pinned upstream, so committing
# ~40 third-party files would add review surface for no provenance gain.
!/.agents/*.md
!/GLOSSARY.md

# --- conventional repository files ---
# None of these three exists yet; the negations are permissions, not files.
# README.md and CONTRIBUTING.md are whitelisted here by explicit directive even
# though AGENTS.md §4.6 currently says "no README.md or other root-level
# document is authorized" — a contradiction recorded in MEMORY.md ADL-0024
# rather than resolved unilaterally here, because the two documents disagree
# about intent and only one of them is a code contract.
!/README.md
!/CONTRIBUTING.md

# LICENSE has no .md extension, so the rule above never matches it. It is named
# anyway, because a reader of this file should not have to work that out: the
# complete set of tracked documentation-adjacent files is the seven, these two,
# and the licence.
!/LICENSE
